alt: (Alternator: def"
An alternator is a device that turns angular momentum into AC Electricity. (ME = AC))
(input: mv, rpm;)
(output: vac, hz;)
(dimensions:
(master: (pulley: radius, width, depth, material;)(gear: radius, width, teeth count, teeth depth, material;))
(housing: outside diameter, inside diameter, length;)
(stator: poles, windings, coil material;)(rotor: poles, windings, coil material, shaft radius;))
(equation: )

em: (Electric Motor: def"
An electric motor is a device that converts electrical energy into mechanical energy.
Its function is governed by the causal relationship. (Ec) = (ME);)
(input: (dc: vdc;)(ac: vac, hz;))
(ouput: mv, rpm;)
(DC:
(bm: (brushed_motor: def"
A simple electric motor that uses brushes to deliver current to the motor windings.;)
(dimensions:
(stator: permanent magnet;)
(rotor: armature;)
(slave:
(pulley: radius, width, depth, material;)
(gear: radius, width, teeth count, teeth depth, material;))
equation: Ec:brushed = ME:shaft;))
(blm: (brushless_motor: def"
A more efficient electric motor that uses electronic commutation instead of brushes.;)
(stator: )
(rotor: )
(slave:
(pulley: radius, width, depth, material;)
(gear: radius, width, teeth count, teeth depth, material;))
(equation: Ec:brushless = ME:shaft;)))
(AC:
(sm: (Synchronous Motor: def"
A Synchronous AC Motor uses an electro-magnetic rotor that synchronizes with the hz.;)
(dimensions:
(housing: outside diameter, length;)
(stator: poles, windings, coil material;)
(rotor: poles, windings, coil material, shaft radius;)
(slave:
(pulley: radius, width, depth, material;)
(gear: radius, width, teeth count, teeth depth, material;))
(equation: ))
(im: (Induction Motor: def"
An AC Induction Motor uses an iron rotor to induce a magnetic field that is manipulated by the phases.;)
(dimensions:
(housing: outside diameter, length;)
(stator: poles, windings, coil material;)
(rotor: poles, material;)
(slave:
(pulley: radius, width, depth, material;)
(gear: radius, width, teeth count, teeth depth, material;))
(equation: )
))

ewp: (Electric Water Pump: def"
A device that uses electricity to move water. (DC = ME = FD))
(input: (ac: vac, hz;)(dc: vdc;))
(output: (fm, psi, gpm))
(em[>em])
(housing: inside diameter, outside diameter, outside height, inside height, inlet, outlet, material;)
(impeller: radius, blade count, blade width, blade height, shaft radius, shaft height, material;)